DOCLING PDF EXTRACTION

Docling is the PDF extractor. It runs in a separately managed environment rather
than being installed into the app's environment.

    Docling 2.135.0 (MIT License)
    https://pypi.org/project/docling/
    https://github.com/docling-project/docling

    rapidocr 3.9.1 (Apache License 2.0)
    https://pypi.org/project/rapidocr/
    https://github.com/RapidAI/RapidOCR

The pins are explicit because docling 2.135.0 imports a symbol rapidocr 3.10.0
removed, so docling and rapidocr 3.9.1 install together even though this app runs
with OCR disabled.

Docling is not installed with this app. The first PDF conversion builds a
separate, pinned virtual environment for it under the user cache and runs it
there; the app's own environment never
carries Docling. Docling resolves its own Python dependency chain, which carries
packages under their own licenses; this repository makes no claim about them and
does not relicense them. An online run may fetch Docling's required layout
model artifacts to a local cache lazily on first use, inside the bounded worker;
an offline run never fetches them. Those model files are separate works under
their own licenses, are not redistributed here, and must be reviewed against the
intended use before redistribution. Docling is imported only inside that
separate, resource-bounded worker process; it is never imported into this app's
own process, and OCR, VLM, and enrichment models are disabled in the
configuration this app supplies.

